<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 24 July, from 1132 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1132 CE <span class="tih-ago">894 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Count Ranulf of Alife defeats Roger II of Sicily at Nocera</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Nocera, also called Scafati, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a> fought his first major battle and suffered the first of his two major defeats, at the hands of Count Ranulf II of Alife, the husband of his sister Matilda.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1148 CE <span class="tih-ago">878 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis VII and Conrad III lay siege to Damascus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>, the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france">Louis VII of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-iii-of-germany">Conrad III of Germany</a>, with that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>, laid siege to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>. The siege failed after four days, ending in a crusader defeat.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france">Louis VII of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1411">1411 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">615 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Donald, Lord of the Isles, fights the Earl of Mar at Harlaw</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Inverurie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aberdeenshire">Aberdeenshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donald-lord-of-the-isles">Donald, Lord of the Isles</a>, pressing his wife's claim to the earldom of Ross, led a Highland army against forces raised by Alexander Stewart, Earl of Mar. The battle was indecisive, and Donald withdrew west.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-harlaw">Battle of Harlaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1534">1534 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacques Cartier plants a cross at Gaspé and claims it for France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier">Jacques Cartier</a> raised a nine-metre wooden cross at Gaspé Bay bearing the arms of the King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The gesture began French claims to the St Lawrence region that became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/new-france">New France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier">Jacques Cartier</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1567 CE <span class="tih-ago">459 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots is forced to abdicate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Imprisoned at Lochleven, Mary was compelled to abdicate in favour of her one-year-old son, crowned James VI five days later. She fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1568 and was executed in 1587.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/detroit" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/detroit.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1701">1701 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">325 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac founds Detroit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French officer Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac established Fort Pontchartrain du Détroit on the strait between Lakes Erie and Huron. The trading post grew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a>, later the heart of the US car industry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1847">1847 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brigham Young's Mormon pioneers enter the Salt Lake Valley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long trek from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigham-young">Brigham Young</a>'s vanguard company entered the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-lake-valley">Salt Lake Valley</a>; he reportedly declared 'This is the right place'. Salt Lake City became the centre of the Latter-day Saints.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hiram Bingham reaches the Inca citadel of Machu Picchu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Guided by local farmer Melchor Arteaga, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ial">Yale</a> lecturer Hiram Bingham climbed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/machu-picchu">Machu Picchu</a>, already known to local families. His photographs made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> site world-famous.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court orders Nixon to hand over the Watergate tapes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> v. Nixon the Supreme Court ruled 8-0 that the president must surrender the tapes. Their contents destroyed his remaining support, and he resigned 16 days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 24 July <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-margrave-of-baden-durlach"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-margrave-of-baden-durlach.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II, Margrave of Baden-Durlach</span><span class="tp">1529–1577</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/simon-bolivar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Simón Bolívar</span><span class="tp">1783–1830</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juan-vicente-gomez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juan-vicente-gomez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juan Vicente Gómez</span><span class="tp">1857–1935</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 24 July <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oswulf-of-northumbria"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Oswulf of Northumbria</span><span class="tp">d. 759</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-tuscany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/matilda-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Matilda of Tuscany</span><span class="tp">1046–1115</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jacob-van-artevelde"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jacob-van-artevelde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jacob van Artevelde</span><span class="tp">c. 1290–1345</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
